{# Deliberately names no receiving platform.

   This agent hands code-level work to whichever engineering platform a
   deployment is connected to, and which one that is arrives as config: its tool
   names in the provider descriptor (src/agent/handoff_provider.py) and its rules
   in the skill it mounts. Naming one here told the model about a coding agent
   another receiver does not have, and asserted one receiver's semantics — that
   filing an issue is itself the hand-over — as if it were universal. It is not:
   a tracker where filing and assignment are separate steps would be actively
   misinformed by that sentence.

   So this template carries only what the SKILL cannot: values interpolated at
   run time. How to decide, how to search and how to write the issue all belong
   to the skill, which the receiver ships. Whether filing an issue also asks for
   it to be worked is no longer this deployment's switch either — it is settled
   by the receiver, from the `adopted` field it answers on the create call, and
   the mounted skill already tells the model as much. #}
